<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi Electric surges 14.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Karachi Electric surges 14.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Electric Supply Corporation (KESC) jumped 1.80 rupees, or 14.75 percent, to 14 after an announcement that it would be privatised this year, dealers said.</p>
<p>A turnover of 58,000 shares of the state-owned utility had been recorded at the Karachi Stock Exchange by noon (0700 GMT).</p>
<p>KESC's managing director Shahid Hamid said on Monday that the corporation would be privatised by December.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not new, as the KESC has long been a prime candidate for privatisation,&quot; dealer Ambreen Shaukat said. &quot;But this statement has triggered fresh buying in the stock.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
